 >>[2026-07-27 16:02] observe — Hygiene noise: 45 untracked .d.ts under packages/spw-cli/src and 15 under packages/spw-runtime/src despite outDir=node_modules/.cache/tsbuild. .scratch/ also untracked. git status is nearly unreadable.
 >>[2026-07-27 16:02] observe — directive-lattice cache still planning/next=1 while main already holds particle lexer, fragment resolve, census, reference graph inversion, and neovim modularization. Classic landed-ahead-of-cache.
 >>[2026-07-27 16:02] observe — spw refresh only derives open_count and last_stream. status, next_commit, base_ref remain manual — so ecology truth still depends on agent discipline.
 >>[2026-07-27 16:03] decide — Four pillars as one plan: hygiene floor, doc robustness, plan index, consolidation verbs. Not four micro-plans — they share one ship gate and one census.
 >>[2026-07-27 16:03] decide — This slug is the hygiene split for the hot cluster. Explicitly forbidden: server-index.ts and geometry-inspect.ts edits. Schedule collisions are indexed, not implemented.
 >>[2026-07-27 16:03] decide — apposition-cache-granules before spw-beat-diff-precipitation remains the schedule; surface-identity already rules one workspace cache block. Record only.
 >>[2026-07-27 16:03] taste — Status tokens must stay single tokens (planning|active|review|…). seed-roundness taught that prose-in-cache breaks every ecology reader.
 >>[2026-07-27 16:03] taste — plans/index.spw is a routing table, not a second essay. Doctrine lives in the distilled artifact + plan-ecology-clustering.spw.
 >>[2026-07-27 16:04] note — Tip tools mass/authority/lite have no plan slugs. Consolidation will add stream notes or thin retrospectives so main is not plan-invisible; full feature plans only if work continues.
 >>[2026-07-27 16:10] note — Distilled artifact rewritten for clean parse (quoted prose, list status tokens, no stream-delimiter semis). wip keeps stream convention shared with peer plans.
 >>[2026-07-27 17:20] observe — Language-gap review: soft encodings (freeform key:value ~2k, opaque strings ~1.8k, // comments, dual prose) outcompete products; bias almost unused (~8). Recognition gaps (claim lists, derived marks, holes, wonder-device, shape/granule machines) and vocabulary forks (effect.l* vs S0/E0; hash vs fingerprint vs key) documented.
 >>[2026-07-27 17:20] decide — Filed PLAN.md Appendix A (language gaps and design conflicts) as diagnosis only. Maps four pillars to language roots; lists follow-on seeds (config-binding-product, operator-lifecycle-closeout, canon-layout-single-tree) without scheduling them on this spine. Discipline-now list stays in-scope for authoring under this plan.
 >>[2026-07-27 17:20] taste — Highest leverage without grammar: stop freeform maps for new config, one effect ladder in public surfaces, one structural epistemology per tool, no hand-edited derived cache fields.
 >>[2026-07-27 17:45] implement — Appendix B + references/documentation-referentiality.spw: robustness grades g0-g5, forms_live vs forms_soft, goals_without_strings (erase test), goals_with_dimension (axes + ladder d0-d5), migrate_examples, tool_goals for commit 6. Authoring floor: new docs ≥ d1 path ref, indexes ≥ d2 root alias.
 >>[2026-07-27 17:45] decide — String-erase test is a goal metric for language follow-on, not a hard fail for hygiene commits 2-5. Ship floor for docs pillar remains g1+g2+g5.
 >>[2026-07-27 17:45] taste — Prefer closed tokens for ceilings and status; keep human gloss as ~# aspect beside the token, not inside it.
